 section('formula','How does the salary comparison work?',`<div class="formula-card"><div class="formula">Effective hourly rate = (salary + bonus + 401(k) match − health premiums) ÷ [(work hours + commute hours) × (52 − PTO weeks)]</div><p class="example">($60,000 + $2,000) ÷ [(40 + 5) × 50] = $27.56 per committed hour</p></div>`+para('Enter an employer 401(k) match percentage and the monthly health premium you pay: the match is added to total compensation and the premium is subtracted before dividing by committed hours. Leave both at zero to compare salary and bonus only.')+para('A standard salary-to-hourly conversion divides pay by scheduled work hours only. This comparison goes further: it counts every hour the job takes from your week — including the commute — and removes paid weeks off, when you are paid without committing time.'))
